# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated / re-fetchable data. Rule: if a script can rebuild it, don't track
# it. Everything below is reproducible from the CFBD API (needs CFBD_API_KEY)
# or from the ingest pipeline.
#
# NOTE: gitignore has NO trailing-comment syntax — `foo/  # why` is parsed as a
# pattern containing spaces and a `#`, matching nothing. Comments go on their
# own line. (This bit once: it staged 822 files and 329M of cache.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# raw HTTP response cache, 329M
cfbd_cache/

# per-year/category API dumps, gather_rb_data.py rebuilds, 12M
cfbd_data/

# TS ingest output, `npm run ingest` rebuilds, 80M
data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LICENSED THIRD-PARTY DATA — never commit.
#
# PFF Ultimate exports, pulled under Stanford's team license. Unlike everything
# else here this is NOT excluded because it is regenerable; it is excluded
# because it is licensed and redistribution is not ours to grant. The assistant
# GM signed off on a shareable derived file, which is a different thing from
# publishing PFF's rows. Derived model coefficients and labels are fine to
# commit; these source CSVs are not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
pff_data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TRACKED ON PURPOSE, listed here so nobody "cleans them up":
#   yearly_wr_te_outcomes.csv   } model inputs. Regenerable but slow, and
#   yearly_rb_outcomes.csv      } app.py needs them for a clean-clone run
#   yearly_player_outcomes.csv  } (PDR §4.1). 6.2M total.
#   Player Data/                hand-supplied source CSVs, NOT script-regenerable
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

